From 862864503e410cbd144955142d19a31330762a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rust-rounds): keep a take per speak-to point, and judge
 it by its point (RR24)

A week's ticket is answered point by point (paulgsc/some-ui#3248, the
owner's approval of the RR24 prototype, 2026-11-19): each speak-to point
gets a take of its own, recorded, redone and let go on its own. The point
is read from the take's ref, `<week>:<ticket>:<n>` from 1, never split
from a take or guessed. A take of the whole ticket (`<week>:<ticket>`)
stays valid for good and answers every point, judged as before.

- voice: `is_rust_round_ref` takes `<week>:<ticket>:<n>` (n 1-99, no
  leading zero); `about` names the point (`Detail::RustRound.point`).
- week: each ticket's speak-to count (`TicketProgram.points`), read from
  `speakTo`'s length, nothing tied to 3.
- sent: `Answer.point`, optional, and absent from a phone before RR24; a
  ticket is answered whole, point by point or both, each at most once, and
  a point must be one of its ticket's.
- record and the routine's index: `TicketRecord.points`, each point
  answered on its own; `take` stays the whole ticket's.
- essay: a point answered on its own is the essay's item `<ticket>.<n>`
  (`tickets[i].points[j].answer`), played as `takes/<ticket>.<n>.<ext>`;
  `against` holds it to the final as it does a ticket.
- CONTRACT_EPOCH 19 -> 20 (the phone records per point only from it);
  RENDER_FOLDERS_EPOCH 1 -> 2 (point takes in `takes/`).

Refs paulgsc/some-ui#3248

